 "library": {
  "title": "4-high electrode calendering line, 1.5 m, roll-to-roll with web path",
  "description": "Roll-to-roll calendering line for battery electrodes (lab/pilot scale). Machine about 1500 x 400 (frame) x 640 mm; control cabinet (300 x 600 x 1160) stands beside the rewind end, HMI pole at the front. Web 300 mm wide runs left to right at a 300 mm pass line: unwind reel (dia 160, brake, belt drive) -> idler -> pneumatic dancer -> idler -> edge-guide sensor -> load-cell tension roll -> spreader roll -> entry idler -> 4-high calender stand (two dia 100 work rolls with 2 mm nip, two dia 140 backup rolls, chocks in 40 mm housings, hydraulic roll-force cylinders, hot-oil rotary joints, drive spindles with meshing pinion gears, gearbox and main motor) -> chill roll (dia 120) -> S-wrap rolls -> thickness gauge -> rewind dancer -> idler -> rewind reel. The web is a precomputed tangent-and-arc polygon wrapping each roll on the correct side (regenerate if rolls move). Drive side (+Y): timing belts, pulleys, tensioner and gear train. Variables: D, WW, WR, BR, GAP, ZN, RE. Transparent front plates, E-stops, nip guard, levelling feet.",
  "tags": [
   "calender",
